answers.body:
By default, nested parallelism is not turned on in OpenMP (at least before version 5.0). So if you do this for e.g.: #pragma omp parallel for
for(int i = 0; i < N; i++) {
  #pragma omp parallel for
  for(int j = 0; j < N; j++) {
     // Some work
  }
} then the inner loop is not parallelised, despite the presence of the #pragma statement. If it's enabled by setting OMP_NESTED to true , you can turn it off/on selectively within your code by using omp_set_nested

