Seems that the code snippet with the race condition used in my class has been copied from other sources.  I am concurrently reading The OpenMP Common Core [1] and found a race-free equivalent using atomic as recommended by @MichaelKlemm.  I modified my original snippet based on Figure 11.5 in [1]. #pragma omp parallel shared(data, flag)
{
    int temp = 0;

    if (omp_get_thread_num() == 0) {  // Producer.
        // Write to data and make visible to other thread.
        data = computeData();
        #pragma omp flush

        // Write to flag with atomic results in implicit flush.
        #pragma omp atomic write
        flag = 1;
    }   
    if (omp_get_thread_num() == 1) {  // Consumer.
        while (!temp) {
            #pragma omp atomic read
            temp = flag;              // Read into temp in case flag changes.
        }   
        #pragma omp flush
        f(data);                      // Do something with data.
    }   
} [1] https://mitpress.mit.edu/books/openmp-common-core

